    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d298-a14">

                <pb facs="0790" n="668" sameAs="frus:frus1889/pg668"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 14 in No. 27.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Williams to Mr.
                            Pierce.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Consulate-General of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Havana</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-12-26"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >December</hi> 26, 1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: After writing my letter to you on the 22d
                    instant in relation to the fine of $800 imposed on the steamer <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Manhattan</hi> for the alleged 4 tierces of lard not
                    delivered according to manifest, I had a visit from and an interview upon the
                    subject with Capt. Frank Stevens, the commander of that steamer, and he tells me
                    that he delivered his cargo all right that trip, and that the dispute pending
                    originated in a private matter of Messrs. Bea, Bellido &amp; Co. As this is a
                    question of a fine imposed upon an American ship in your consular district, and
                    the information of it having been communicated by you to this office for the
                    first time five months after it occurred, and as in the regular course of
                    business it must be reported to the Department of State, you will please
                    communicate to me whatever facts are on record at your office tending to
                    exculpate the steamer</p>
                <p>I am, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Ramon O.
                    Williams.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
